  "rules": [
    "Systematic Underestimation of Spikes: The model consistently fails to capture the magnitude of upward price breaks (e.g., the jump from ~81 to ~88 in late November), resulting in a persistent negative bias during breakout phases.",
    "Excessive Mean Reversion Lag: Forecasts exhibit a slow decay after price peaks, maintaining elevated levels for 10-15 days longer than actual prices, which then crash sharply. The model lacks the volatility to predict the speed of the subsequent correction.",
    "Sentiment Ignorance: Positive sentiment spikes (values > 0.20) are not weighted sufficiently in the forecast, leading to a failure to anticipate immediate price surges that follow positive news.",
    "Horizon-Specific Overshoot: In the 15-20 day horizon, the model predicts a plateau or slow decline, whereas the true outcome shows a steep drop followed by a secondary rebound, indicating a structural error in modeling the post-peak volatility regime."
  ]
}
